      "writtenOn": "2026-10-13T16:37:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not suggesting a git bisect right away. Let\u0027s assume Clang 22.0.1 was broken and 22.0.2 contains the fix.\n\nI\u0027d take an older kernel revision that was 100% confirmed working with Clang before 22.0.1, remove the version pin, and rebuild those exact sources with the fixed Clang 22.0.2.\n\nIf it boots while the current kernel doesn\u0027t, that points to a regression introduced by later kernel changes. Then we can use git bisect to find the culprit.\n\nThe idea is simply to establish a known-good baseline before digging any deeper.",
      "parentUuid": "bfa5494b_98e86803",
      "revId": "6fc3b9848df497bbb38986cd8502d8a765ba844a",
